package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Compute.Math
use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.Shapes.Triangle

/*
A box turned 45 degrees about z, so its bottom edge runs along z at
height -0.25 times the square root of 2, above a triangle standing on
end whose top edge runs along x at -0.38. The two edges cross, so the
contact is where they cross, and the normal is straight up.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleEdgeDirectionTest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: edge pair direction")
    end

    action Run
        Math math
        Triangle triangle
        triangle:Set(MakeVector(-1, -0.38, 0), MakeVector(1, -0.38, 0), MakeVector(0, -1, 0))
        triangle:SetMargin(0.04)
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(triangle, MakeTransform(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 45), false)
        number edgeHeight = -0.25 * math:SquareRoot(2)
        CheckContact("box edge direction", points, 0, -1, 0, 0, edgeHeight, 0, 0.38 + edgeHeight - 0.04)
    end
end
